    "description": "Vintage Hoya & Albinar Camera Lens Lot\nMixed Focal Lengths, Japanese & Korean Optics\nIncluding Auto Extension Tube Set\nThis vintage photography equipment lot features a versatile collection of optics and accessories designed for manual focus SLR systems. The set includes a high-reach Hoya telephoto zoom lens, a specialized Albinar-ADG super wide fish-eye optic for creative distortion, and a complete AT-5 auto extension tube set for macro photography. These items represent the robust third-party manufacturing era of the late 20th century, providing photographers with expanded creative capabilities for portraiture, landscapes, and close-up work.\nHoya Telephoto Zoom Lens - Model 6020-1076, 52mm filter thread, features a diamond-texture rubberized grip and manual aperture control\nAlbinar-ADG Super Wide Fish-eye Lens - Model 6020-0201, designed for wide-angle distortion effects and creative perspective\nAT-5 Auto Extension Tube Set - Three-piece modular set including 12mm, 20mm, and 36mm tubes for varying macro magnification levels\nIncludes two cylindrical protective lens cases and one rectangular hard case for the extension tubes\nCondition:\nLens barrels show light handling wear with minimal paint loss on the edges. Glass elements appear clear with no visible fungus, haze, or major scratches. Aperture blades on both lenses appear clean and responsive. Extension tubes show no signs of corrosion or mount damage. Protective cases are intact with functional closures. Functionality not confirmed; lenses not tested with a camera body.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
